{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$f$ is the derivative of $F$, which means $F$ is an antiderivative of $f$.\n\nSince we know the antiderivative of $f$, we can use the fundamental theorem of calculus: For every function $f$ and its antiderivative $F$,\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx=F(b)-F(a)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\int_{-5}^{5} f(x)\\,dx\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=F(\\blueD{5})-F(\\blueD{-5})\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=|4\\blueD{(5)}-20|-|4\\blueD{(-5)}-20|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=0-40\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-40\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-5}^{5} f(x)\\,dx=-40$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026F(x)=|4x-20|\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026f(x)=F'(x)\n\\end{align}$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-5}^{5} f(x)\\,dx=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":-40}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"definite integral","size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
